      "message": "Done -- trimmed from 79 lines to 56: dropped the diagnostic\ncounts, the remaining-warnings inventory and most of the architecture\nbackground, keeping problem / solution / validation.\n\nOn splitting out the warning cleanups: I\u0027d rather keep them here, if you\ndon\u0027t mind. They are the same sweep over the same emitters -- the\n-Wsign-compare loop counters are literally the same forloop templates the\nalignment fix rewrites, so splitting produces two changes that conflict in\nevery hunk, and each one needs the full 151-header regeneration plus a tree\nbuild to validate. I\u0027ve made the message say plainly which part is the fix\nand which is the cleanup. Happy to split if you still prefer it after\nlooking at patch set 3.",
