      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, and fixed. You\u0027re right that the cast was emitted for\neverything outside FORMAT_STRINGS, so aggregate call sites started passing\nvoid * to formatters that still va_arg a typed pointer -- formally\nincompatible per C11 7.16.1.1p2, and a regression I introduced rather than\nanything pre-existing.\n\nBoth sites now gate on scalar_needs_alignment(), so only scalar and enum\nformatters -- the ones whose signature actually changed to void * -- get the\ncast (print_field line 1026, print_array line 1085). Verified on a fixture\ncarrying both kinds:\n\n  format_vl_api_myindex_t, (void *) \u0026a-\u003escalar_field     \u003c- scalar, cast\n  format_vl_api_myagg_t, \u0026a-\u003eagg_field                   \u003c- aggregate, typed\n\nAggregates keep the typed form for the reason you\u0027d expect: they\u0027re packed,\nalignof is 1, so a pointer to a misaligned one was never a problem.",
      "parentUuid": "82dcfdbc_2ad9e8e2",
      "revId": "233f8c4e4394529d0c5a4acf95cf44c124ddf102",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
